# 14. Connecting the Training Script to the Server ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐

Our training script now becomes a client of the MLflow server.

```python
import mlflow

mlflow.set_tracking_uri(
    "http://127.0.0.1:5000"
)

mlflow.set_experiment(
    "sre-incident-predictor"
)
```

Then:

```python
with mlflow.start_run():

    mlflow.log_param(
        "max_iter",
        1000
    )

    mlflow.log_metric(
        "accuracy",
        0.91
    )
```

### What changed?

Our training logic did not need to change.

Only the tracking destination changed.

```text
Training Application
        ↓
MLflow Client
        ↓
HTTP Request
        ↓
MLflow Tracking Server
        ↓
PostgreSQL
```

**Mental Model:**

> The training application does not need to know the internal details of PostgreSQL or artifact storage. It interacts with the configured MLflow tracking service.

