# 23. Database Migrations ⭐⭐⭐⭐

MLflow evolves over time.

New versions may introduce changes to the backend database schema.

Therefore, upgrading MLflow can require a database migration.

Example:

```bash
mlflow db upgrade \
  "postgresql+psycopg2://mlflow:password@127.0.0.1:5432/mlflow"
```

The password above is illustrative. In real environments, use secure credential handling.

### Production Upgrade Mental Model

```text
New MLflow Version
        ↓
Compatibility Check
        ↓
Database Backup
        ↓
Test Migration
        ↓
Run Required Migration
        ↓
Deploy New MLflow Version
        ↓
Validate Tracking / Registry
```

### Why is this important?

A database schema migration may not be safely reversible simply by rolling back the MLflow application version.

Therefore:

- Back up the database.
- Test migrations in staging.
- Review release notes.
- Plan downtime or rollout coordination.
- Validate after upgrading.

We cover production upgrades in more detail on Day 5.

