# 25. Common Mistakes

### Mistake 1 — PostgreSQL Stores Model Files

Incorrect:

```text
PostgreSQL
    ↓
Everything, including large model files
```

Correct:

```text
PostgreSQL
    ↓
Metadata

Artifact Store
    ↓
Model Files
```

### Mistake 2 — MLflow Server Healthy Means Platform Healthy

Incorrect:

```text
MLflow /health = 200
        ↓
Everything Healthy
```

Correct:

```text
MLflow API Healthy
        +
PostgreSQL Healthy
        +
Artifact Access Working
        +
Registry Operations Working
        ↓
Functional Platform Health
```

### Mistake 3 — PostgreSQL Automatically Makes MLflow HA

PostgreSQL provides a durable shared backend, but HA requires replication, failover and appropriate operational configuration.

### Mistake 4 — Local Artifacts Are Production-Ready

Local artifact directories are useful for development.

Shared production deployments generally need durable storage accessible to all relevant MLflow instances.

### Mistake 5 — All Artifact Traffic Always Passes Through MLflow

MLflow supports both proxied and direct artifact access patterns.

The chosen configuration determines the actual data path.

### Mistake 6 — Application Rollback Always Reverses DB Migrations

A schema migration can require a separate recovery procedure.

